// TEMPLATE: framework ATTACHMENT-resource skeleton — codegen subtype
// "attachment" (bind/unbind relation with a composite parent#child id).
//
// Structural skeleton shared with general_template.go.tmpl; the differences
// are all attachment-specific and marked with TEMPLATE notes below:
//   - Create = bind API(s); Delete = unbind API(s); Update is a no-op body
//     (every mutable attribute is RequiresReplace — attachments are
//     force-recreated, never updated in place);
//   - the composite id comes from the codegen JSON's resource_id
//     (`#`-joined SDK field names, e.g. "InstanceId#DiskId"): one Required
//     id attribute per segment, joined via fwHelper.IdFormat in the given
//     order — the segment order is ALWAYS parent-first (largest to
//     smallest): in A#B#C, A is the parent of B and B is the parent of C
//     (e.g. "InstanceId#DiskId" because the CVM instance owns the disk —
//     never the reverse order);
//   - Read queries a parent-level describe API and treats "binding absent
//     in the response" as not-found.
//
// Location: tencentcloud/services/<product>/resource_tc_<name>_attachment.go
// (keep the conventional `_attachment` suffix when resource_name ends with
// `_attachment`). Factory naming: New<Product><Name>AttachmentResource.

